WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.306
The earliest event in the Saw timeline is the birth of John Kramer, aka

00:00:03.338 --> 00:00:05.790
Jigsaw in 1953 or 1954.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:09.454
We know this because at the time of his death in 2006, they mention his age.

00:00:09.572 --> 00:00:14.698
-[Doctor] Subject's name is John Kramer, a 52 year old male Caucasian.

00:00:14.794 --> 00:00:17.514
Over the next 30 years, the Saw timeline is pretty uneventful.

00:00:17.562 --> 00:00:19.331
Other than the birth of some major characters.

00:00:19.331 --> 00:00:20.446
We don't have exact dates for

00:00:20.468 --> 00:00:23.198
most of them, but based on their ages in the movies, I'd estimate that

00:00:23.204 --> 00:00:26.838
Lawrence Gordon was born in the 1950s and Mark Hoffman, Eric Matthews and Amanda Young

00:00:26.844 --> 00:00:28.822
were born in the 1960s.

00:00:28.876 --> 00:00:33.718
We do know that Hoffman's sister Angelina was born in 1971 or 1972, which we

00:00:33.724 --> 00:00:36.726
can deduce from a newspaper article showing that she was 25 at the time of

00:00:36.748 --> 00:00:38.038
her death in 1997.

00:00:38.124 --> 00:00:43.014
Then there's Logan Nelson, born August 18, 1973, and

00:00:43.052 --> 00:00:47.018
Steven Singh, born in 1975 or 1976, which we can do the math on based on his age at the time of

00:00:47.024 --> 00:00:48.254
his death in 2004.

00:00:48.254 --> 00:00:54.004
-[Rich] A raid that also resulted in the death of Tapp's partner, 28 year old Stephen Singh.

00:00:54.182 --> 00:00:56.798
While the birth dates of these characters aren't super important to the

00:00:56.804 --> 00:01:00.062
story, I found that I can use similar logic to determine the dates of almost

00:01:00.116 --> 00:01:03.326
everything that happens in the series and create the ultimate timeline that

00:01:03.348 --> 00:01:06.174
can help us better understand everything about the Saw lore and answer

00:01:06.212 --> 00:01:08.158
questions that have always confunded fans.

00:01:08.254 --> 00:01:11.538
So if you want to know the date and order of events of everything in the

00:01:11.544 --> 00:01:14.258
franchise, stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:14.344 --> 00:01:16.760
Thank you to BetterHelp for sponsoring this video.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:22.682
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:26.962
Jigsaw, the titular villain of the Saw saga, is most known for his puzzles.

00:01:27.026 --> 00:01:30.166
In order to solve many of his games and traps, you have to put together the

00:01:30.188 --> 00:01:30.882
puzzle pieces.

00:01:30.946 --> 00:01:34.346
I even did a character analysis episode where I put together the pieces of

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:35.290
Jigsaw's life.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.574
Fittingly the Saw timeline is also a puzzle.

00:01:37.622 --> 00:01:39.126
There are no title cards or graphics.

00:01:39.158 --> 00:01:42.122
To display the dates and the movies are known for their flashbacks within

00:01:42.176 --> 00:01:45.498
flashbacks and non linear storytelling but there are clues hidden

00:01:45.514 --> 00:01:47.629
throughout about when certain things take place.

00:01:47.629 --> 00:01:48.862
If you want to know when

00:01:48.916 --> 00:01:51.866
Dr. Lawrence Gordon graduated from college, for example, you'll have to zoom

00:01:51.898 --> 00:01:55.118
into his diploma behind the desk June 4, 1979.

00:01:55.204 --> 00:01:58.306
This has led many Saw fans to wonder, what if you put everything in

00:01:58.328 --> 00:02:01.602
chronological order? Does the story still work? Or will this create

00:02:01.656 --> 00:02:04.354
paradoxes and contradictions? After all, if Dr. Gordon graduated 

00:02:04.392 --> 00:02:09.152
when his diploma says he did, that makes him probably as old as John Kramer. 

00:02:09.152 --> 00:02:11.454
What I found is that for the most part, the Saw timeline

00:02:11.502 --> 00:02:14.486
is one of the most well thought out and accurate horror movie timelines out there.

00:02:14.508 --> 00:02:17.841
There are a few things that don't make sense, but most of them can be explained.

00:02:17.841 --> 00:02:20.882
Overall, the puzzle pieces actually fit together really nicely,

00:02:20.946 --> 00:02:22.914
and this was a really fun puzzle to solve.

00:02:22.962 --> 00:02:24.986
I know the Saw fans have been asking for this ever since

00:02:25.008 --> 00:02:28.090
I put together a timeline for my horror history episodes a few years ago.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.742
Since then, I've noticed some things and made this timeline even more accurate. 

00:02:31.796 --> 00:02:35.022
So let's take it back to the next point of importance in the Saw

00:02:35.076 --> 00:02:37.200
story the 1980s.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:41.738
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:45.838
It would have likely been somewhere around 1983, when Adam Stanheit, who

00:02:45.844 --> 00:02:48.946
would go on to be a photographer and one of John Kramer's many victims, got

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.134
a preview of that pain on his 6th birthday.

00:02:51.262 --> 00:02:55.458
-[Adam] On my 6th birthday, my best friend at the time, Scott Tibbs,

00:02:55.464 --> 00:02:56.046
-[Adam] a rusty nail.

00:02:56.078 --> 00:02:56.962
-[Adam] I didn't tell you about that.

00:02:57.016 --> 00:03:00.194
Then there's the early career of Detective Mark Hoffman before eventually

00:03:00.242 --> 00:03:02.066
going on to be Jigsaw's first successor.

00:03:02.098 --> 00:03:04.678
He became a cop sometime in the early 1980s.

00:03:04.764 --> 00:03:06.374
-[Mark] I've been a cop for 20 years.

00:03:06.492 --> 00:03:09.734
John Kramer himself went on to be a civil engineer, creating his first

00:03:09.772 --> 00:03:12.934
building, the Gideon Meatpacking Plant, sometime in the mid to late 80s.

00:03:12.972 --> 00:03:15.878
Shortly after this, he teamed up with lawyer Art Blank to start the

00:03:15.894 --> 00:03:17.910
Urban Renewal Group to create low income housing.

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.970
One of these homes is the location later known as the nerve Gas house.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.366
Meanwhile, one of Hoffman's earliest cases involved the investigation of an

00:03:24.388 --> 00:03:26.554
abusive teacher with his partner, Daniel Rigg.

00:03:26.602 --> 00:03:29.774
Things escalate, and Rigg punches the teacher but avoids charges because

00:03:29.812 --> 00:03:31.082
Hoffman lies on his behalf.

00:03:31.146 --> 00:03:32.106
Don't get any ideas.

00:03:32.138 --> 00:03:34.090
No punching the Horror History professor.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:35.486
That is, if you want to live.

00:03:35.588 --> 00:03:39.418
Sometime around 1990, Metropolitan Police Detective Eric Matthews and his

00:03:39.444 --> 00:03:40.862
wife have a son named Daniel.

00:03:40.926 --> 00:03:43.506
We don't have any clues to his date of birth other than the fact that he

00:03:43.528 --> 00:03:45.906
seems to be around 15 years old during the Nerve Gas House Game in 2005.

00:03:45.928 --> 00:03:49.346
Around the time of Daniel's birth, the marital troubles start for

00:03:49.368 --> 00:03:52.534
Eric and his wife, likely due to Eric's infidelity.

00:03:52.572 --> 00:03:55.042
Sometime in the early 90s, Hohn meets his future wife, Jill Tuck.

00:03:55.106 --> 00:03:57.602
Jill is a doctor who works with recovering drug addicts.

00:03:57.666 --> 00:04:00.114
She starts her own practice called Homeward Bound Clinic.

00:04:00.162 --> 00:04:04.054
The movie Homeward Bound was released in 1993, so one might assume that

00:04:04.102 --> 00:04:05.990
Jill was trying to capitalize off that popularity.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:08.538
It makes sense that this would also be around the time that she founded the

00:04:08.544 --> 00:04:11.370
clinic, which was opened before she got pregnant in 1994.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.542
The clinic's motto is cherish your life, a phrase that John would later

00:04:14.596 --> 00:04:15.962
repeat to some of his victims.

00:04:16.026 --> 00:04:17.498
No wonder they were soulmates.

00:04:17.594 --> 00:04:20.906
Jill holds a party at her clinic, where John meets insurance company mogul

00:04:20.938 --> 00:04:21.722
William Easton.

00:04:21.786 --> 00:04:25.086
John doesn't like how William uses a formula to determine who gets health

00:04:25.108 --> 00:04:27.210
coverage and essentially who lives and dies.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:30.638
John isn't a psychopath yet, so William avoids going on his list.

00:04:30.724 --> 00:04:32.398
For now, we'll revisit this.

00:04:32.484 --> 00:04:35.286
The reason that we know all of this takes place in the early 90s is because

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:38.290
John and Jill plan to have a baby in the Chinese year of the pig.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:41.238
John plots it this way because the pig is a symbol of rebirth, which is

00:04:41.244 --> 00:04:42.870
central to both John and Jill's work.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.586
The Year of the Pig occurs every twelve years, meaning that these events

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:48.310
occur in either 1995 or 2007.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:52.474
John does not survive to 2007, so it has to be 1995, meaning their son

00:04:52.512 --> 00:04:56.406
Gideon was likely conceived in April 1994, nine months before

00:04:56.438 --> 00:04:56.938
the Chinese New Year.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:00.326
While Jill is pregnant, John becomes increasingly concerned about her safety

00:05:00.358 --> 00:05:03.626
on the job, noticing some suspicious patients at her clinic, specifically a

00:05:03.648 --> 00:05:06.846
man named Cecil Adams, who John one day had to convince to put away his

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:08.042
knife during an altercation.

00:05:08.106 --> 00:05:11.214
The incident foreshadows the tragic night where everything changes in

00:05:11.252 --> 00:05:12.590
November of 1994.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.838
We know this because John states that Jill was seven months pregnant at the time.

00:05:15.844 --> 00:05:17.226
-[John] This is my wife.

00:05:17.258 --> 00:05:17.882
-[John] She's pregnant.

00:05:17.946 --> 00:05:19.938
-[Doctor]How far along? 
-[John] Seven months.

00:05:20.024 --> 00:05:23.058
While Jill is locking up for the night, Cecil threatens her at knifepoint so

00:05:23.064 --> 00:05:24.254
that he can steal some meds.

00:05:24.302 --> 00:05:27.346
He storms out and slams the door into Jill's stomach, causing her to miscarry.

00:05:27.368 --> 00:05:30.786
The loss of his son devastates John, sending him into a dark

00:05:30.818 --> 00:05:34.066
depression where he distances himself from his wife and his work, causing

00:05:34.098 --> 00:05:35.890
his marriage to slowly fall apart.

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:39.986
On January 31, 1995, during the previously mentioned Year of the Pig celebration

00:05:40.018 --> 00:05:43.754
John donning a pig mask kidnaps Cecil, making him his first victim.

00:05:43.792 --> 00:05:46.650
Just be glad he didn't choose Year of the Rooster, I guess.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:48.598
Those masks are strangely terrifying.

00:05:48.694 --> 00:05:52.182
Cecil awakens in John's workshop, where he takes part in John's first trap,

00:05:52.246 --> 00:05:52.934
the Knife Chair.

00:05:52.982 --> 00:05:56.206
He manages to escape that one, but he tries to retaliate landing him in the

00:05:56.228 --> 00:05:58.730
razor wire cage where he ultimately met his fate.

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:02.062
This is where we first see John cut a jigsaw piece out of Cecil's body,

00:06:02.116 --> 00:06:06.174
which would eventually earn him the nickname Jigsaw and inspire the 1997

00:06:06.212 --> 00:06:08.002
Will Smith song Getting Jiggy With It.

00:06:08.056 --> 00:06:10.297
All I can say is it better be in Saw X.

00:06:10.297 --> 00:06:12.210
Jill attempts to give John another chance.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:15.566
After months of him distancing himself and joined by Art Blank, she visits

00:06:15.598 --> 00:06:17.694
him at his workshop at Gideon Meatpacking Plant.

00:06:17.742 --> 00:06:20.422
John seemingly hasn't recovered at all and kicks them out.

00:06:20.476 --> 00:06:24.198
Jill tried to go back one more time alone but didn't make any progress, and

00:06:24.204 --> 00:06:26.230
this was effectively the end of their relationship.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:29.798
I'm guessing these were still both in early 1995, because when Jill goes the

00:06:29.804 --> 00:06:32.518
second time, there are still reconnaissance photos of Cecil lying around.

00:06:32.604 --> 00:06:35.558
We can also see at this point he's already started working on designing some

00:06:35.564 --> 00:06:38.406
of the famous traps which he would use later on, such as the rack and the

00:06:38.428 --> 00:06:39.154
glass coffin.

00:06:39.202 --> 00:06:41.502
These traps almost most never come to fruition though.

00:06:41.556 --> 00:06:44.282
Shortly after Jill leaves him, John is diagnosed with cancer.

00:06:44.346 --> 00:06:47.806
The combination of a miscarriage, divorce, and cancer diagnosis is too much

00:06:47.828 --> 00:06:50.910
for him to handle, and he decides to drive off a cliff and end his life.

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:52.954
But against all odds, he survives.

00:06:53.002 --> 00:06:56.286
And this near death experience makes him appreciate life in a way that he

00:06:56.308 --> 00:06:57.186
never had before.

00:06:57.288 --> 00:07:00.946
His faith in the rehabilitation method he had tried and failed on Cecil was restored.

00:07:00.968 --> 00:07:04.594
This was still nearly a decade before the events of Saw, but

00:07:04.632 --> 00:07:08.066
despite that, there are still a lot of events to unpack before that fateful

00:07:08.098 --> 00:07:11.590
day when he put himself face down on the bathroom floor.

