Clear Dawn Hospital Game, where he and his team are

00:34:09.334 --> 00:34:12.138
ironically forced to survive a Jigsaw game much like Bobby claimed he had in his book.

00:34:12.224 --> 00:34:15.466
Meanwhile, through a series of clues, Hoffman leads Matt Gibson to his hideout, 

00:34:15.488 --> 00:34:18.394
where a motion activated turret is waiting for him, and Hoffman

00:34:18.442 --> 00:34:20.670
finally gets the revenge he promised all those years ago.

00:34:20.740 --> 00:34:23.546
Hoffman hides inside of a body bag to sneak his way into the police station,

00:34:23.578 --> 00:34:26.706
where he takes out many officers en route to the last person he needs to get

00:34:26.728 --> 00:34:28.190
revenge on, Jill Tuck.

00:34:28.270 --> 00:34:32.098
He sets her up in an old classic, the Reverse Bear Trap, and third time's a

00:34:32.104 --> 00:34:33.118
charm with that device.

00:34:33.214 --> 00:34:36.786
Finally, after seven movies, we get to see it tear someone's face apart from

00:34:36.808 --> 00:34:37.304
the inside.

00:34:37.304 --> 00:34:38.862
And it is so satisfying.

00:34:38.926 --> 00:34:40.590
But Hoffman is still on the loose!

00:34:40.670 --> 00:34:43.846
He packs up some money and guns so he can start a new life, and it blows up

00:34:43.868 --> 00:34:45.026
his hideout in the air hangar.

00:34:45.058 --> 00:34:47.542
But he's intercepted by Jigsaw's greatest asset,

00:34:47.596 --> 00:34:50.870
Dr. Lawrence Gordon, and two more unknown apprentices in pig masks.

00:34:50.950 --> 00:34:54.506
After sedating Detective Hoffman well, I guess we can't call him that

00:34:54.528 --> 00:34:55.894
anymore. I assume he's fired.

00:34:55.942 --> 00:34:59.110
But after sedating Hoffman, gordon locks him inside the bathroom.

00:34:59.190 --> 00:35:00.362
Yes, that bathroom.

00:35:00.426 --> 00:35:02.830
But this time with no chance to escape.

00:35:02.830 --> 00:35:03.616
-[Dr. Gordon] Game over!

00:35:03.616 --> 00:35:05.844
-[Hoffman] No!!!!!

00:35:06.370 --> 00:35:08.606
And for a while, it was game over.

00:35:08.708 --> 00:35:12.406
But aren't you forgetting about someone, one month later, conveniently

00:35:12.458 --> 00:35:15.406
missing out on the whole bloody sauce saga? Logan Nelson would be released

00:35:15.438 --> 00:35:17.122
from his PTSD treatment by Dr. Perry.

00:35:17.176 --> 00:35:20.850
But I would say that he was anything but cured.

00:35:20.850 --> 00:35:23.750
(IMPACT)

00:35:26.715 --> 00:35:29.540
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:35:29.830 --> 00:35:34.166
On October 5th, 2007, Logan Nelson was awarded a Purple Heart, an award given to

00:35:34.572 --> 00:35:36.962
U.S. Military personnel who were wounded or killed in battle.

00:35:37.026 --> 00:35:40.406
For the next eight years, there are no Jigsaw related killings that we know

00:35:40.428 --> 00:35:42.342
about, and things would go back to normal.

00:35:42.406 --> 00:35:44.870
But normal doesn't necessarily mean quiet.

00:35:44.950 --> 00:35:48.106
We don't know exactly when, but Logan got the job as the medical examiner at

00:35:48.128 --> 00:35:49.222
St. Peter's Hospital.

00:35:49.286 --> 00:35:51.882
From this position, he would see a lot of incompetence from the

00:35:51.936 --> 00:35:53.302
local detective Brad Halloran.

00:35:53.366 --> 00:35:56.766
Criminals seemed to go free, while many innocent people ended up dead on

00:35:56.788 --> 00:35:57.482
Logan's table.

00:35:57.546 --> 00:36:01.066
In 2009, on the south side of the city, a new Metro police detective named

00:36:01.098 --> 00:36:04.606
Zeke Banks was partnered with Officer Peter Dunleavy under a policy called

00:36:04.628 --> 00:36:07.598
Article Eight, cops had the power to do essentially whatever they wanted in

00:36:07.604 --> 00:36:10.462
the name of stopping crime, which led to a lot of corruption in the force.

00:36:10.526 --> 00:36:13.522
One day, Dunleavy shot a witness who was planning to testify against another

00:36:13.576 --> 00:36:14.942
officer just to keep him quiet.

00:36:15.006 --> 00:36:18.126
The victim's son, William Emerson, witnessed the crime and came to praise

00:36:18.158 --> 00:36:21.234
Zeke when he did the right thing by reporting Dunleavy to Internal Affairs.

00:36:21.282 --> 00:36:24.518
I'm putting this in 2009 because it's twelve years before the main events of

00:36:24.524 --> 00:36:26.006
Spiral in 2021.

00:36:26.108 --> 00:36:27.564
-[Angie] It's been twelve years? 

00:36:27.746 --> 00:36:34.890
-[Det. Banks] Yes, twelve years.Twelve years ago, I turn in a dirty cop, I get a medal for it.

00:36:34.960 --> 00:36:36.090
-[Det. Banks] Big deal.

00:36:36.160 --> 00:36:39.882
Well, at one point, the son, William Emerson, says it's 15 years.

00:36:40.016 --> 00:36:44.918
-[William] I've been loyal to you since the first day we met 15 years ago.

00:36:45.024 --> 00:36:47.274
-[William] The day your partner killed my father.

00:36:47.402 --> 00:36:50.014
So it looks like another error there, but I'm going to assume it's twelve years,

00:36:50.052 --> 00:36:52.894
because that's said more often, and also 15 years

00:36:52.932 --> 00:36:53.630
doesn't make sense.

00:36:53.700 --> 00:36:57.166
That would put the Dunleavy incident in 2006, and we never saw any of those

00:36:57.188 --> 00:36:58.586
characters during the Saw saga.

00:36:58.618 --> 00:37:01.299
Hoffman even claimed that he was the last one left at one point. 

00:37:01.299 --> 00:37:04.666
In 2011, a degenerate gambler named Malcolm Neal was partially

00:37:04.698 --> 00:37:07.222
responsible responsible for the death of his wife when people he owed money

00:37:07.276 --> 00:37:08.658
broke into his home and slit

00:37:08.674 --> 00:37:09.442
Mrs. Neal's throat.

00:37:09.506 --> 00:37:11.490
This put him in Logan's bad graces.

00:37:11.570 --> 00:37:14.646
It must have happened in 2011, because it's stated to be five years before

00:37:14.668 --> 00:37:17.666
the main events of Jigsaw, which are most likely in 2016.

00:37:17.778 --> 00:37:18.754
-[Logan] Malcolm Neal.

00:37:18.882 --> 00:37:20.086
-[Logan] I remember that case.

00:37:20.188 --> 00:37:21.794
-[Logan] His wife was murdered five years ago.

00:37:21.852 --> 00:37:25.126
Malcolm Neal probably wasn't enough to convince Logan to hold his own Jigsaw

00:37:25.158 --> 00:37:26.938
game, but what would happen next would.

00:37:27.024 --> 00:37:31.206
In 2014, Logan's wife, Christine Nelson, was killed by a loose meth addict

00:37:31.238 --> 00:37:34.814
named Edgar Munson, not to be confused with burnout Eddie Munson from

00:37:34.852 --> 00:37:35.646
Stranger Things.

00:37:35.748 --> 00:37:39.258
To make matters even worse, Munson was free because of a failed conviction

00:37:39.274 --> 00:37:40.442
by Detective Halloran.

00:37:40.506 --> 00:37:43.354
2014 is two years before the main events of Jigsaw.

00:37:43.402 --> 00:37:45.274
-[Det Hunt] It's been two years since Christine passed.

00:37:45.322 --> 00:37:48.834
This was probably the tipping point, and Logan decided to recreate 

00:37:48.872 --> 00:37:52.226
John Kramer's Barn Game to punish Halloran and test himself to see if he could be

00:37:52.248 --> 00:37:53.918
as good of a Jigsaw as his master.

00:37:54.014 --> 00:37:58.210
So in 2016, he holds his own, which I'll call Logan Nelson's Barn Game,

00:37:58.280 --> 00:38:01.766
because what the else would I call it? This is stated several times to be

00:38:01.788 --> 00:38:03.378
ten years after John's death.

00:38:03.474 --> 00:38:04.902
-[Ryan] Kramer's been dead for ten years.

00:38:04.956 --> 00:38:07.574
-[Logan] John Kramer's dead and has been for ten years.

00:38:07.692 --> 00:38:11.478
-[Lab Tech] This is a blood sample, a perp, taken a decade ago.

00:38:11.564 --> 00:38:15.082
There's a bit of a contradiction when Nelson says that John's original game,

00:38:15.136 --> 00:38:18.410
which he did as a secret test before all the other games, was ten years ago.

00:38:18.480 --> 00:38:22.554
Jigsaw died three years after John Kramer's barn game, so they can't both be

00:38:22.592 --> 00:38:23.370
ten years ago.

00:38:23.440 --> 00:38:25.298
It's likely that Nelson was generalizing.

00:38:25.334 --> 00:38:27.870
He was essentially saying this was all about a decade ago.

00:38:27.940 --> 00:38:31.290
Or maybe his PTSD from the war has really affected his math skills.

00:38:31.370 --> 00:38:34.366
Actually, we kind of know that he's using the term ten years ago kind of

00:38:34.388 --> 00:38:36.206
loosely, because he also says this

00:38:36.206 --> 00:38:38.980
-[Logan] Ten years ago, I came out of the war a broken man. 

00:38:38.980 --> 00:38:41.742
Except his file says that he came out of the war in 2005.

00:38:41.796 --> 00:38:46.716
So clearly Nelson is just clumping that whole time period between 2003 and 2006 together in his mind.

00:38:47.370 --> 00:38:50.486
Anyway, Nelson puts three contestants in his version of the Barn Game and

00:38:50.508 --> 00:38:53.522
deposits the bodies in public for Halloran to find after each death.

00:38:53.586 --> 00:38:56.210
Each of them is someone connected to Halloran's past cases.

00:38:56.290 --> 00:38:59.666
He also ends up framing Halloran by leaving the puzzle pieces in his freezer

00:38:59.698 --> 00:39:02.234
and leading him to the pig farm, where the two of them would be the final players.

00:39:02.272 --> 00:39:05.638
And Halloran is scared into confessing all of his dirty police

00:39:05.654 --> 00:39:07.396
work, which Logan gets an audio recording of

00:39:07.396 --> 00:39:09.222
-[Logan] Some will think it's Jigsaw.

00:39:09.286 --> 00:39:10.410
-[Logan] Some will suspect you.

00:39:10.480 --> 00:39:12.410
-[Logan] But no one will suspect me.

00:39:12.480 --> 00:39:15.934
And with all the evidence he needs, logan slices Halloran's head into seven

00:39:15.972 --> 00:39:17.946
pieces with this laser cutter device.

00:39:18.058 --> 00:39:21.226
He would not be the only person to try to hold his own Jigsaw games however.

00:39:21.258 --> 00:39:24.474
William Emerson, the boy who watched his father fall to the corrupt

00:39:24.522 --> 00:39:26.778
police force, was grown up and wanted revenge.

00:39:26.874 --> 00:39:30.114
That takes us to Spiral, where corrupt police officers on the South Side

00:39:30.152 --> 00:39:33.918
Metro PD come to find themselves, one by one, caught in a series of traps.

00:39:34.014 --> 00:39:37.090
I'm placing the beginning of Spiral on July 4th, 2021.

00:39:37.160 --> 00:39:38.690
The July 4 part is obvious.

00:39:38.760 --> 00:39:41.138
It happens during an American Independence Day celebration.

00:39:41.234 --> 00:39:44.498
My calculations on the year are a little less scientific.

00:39:44.594 --> 00:39:47.718
At one point, we see the file of Detective Marv Bozwick, and it says he was

00:39:47.724 --> 00:39:49.542
born on May 9th, 1981.

00:39:49.596 --> 00:39:53.686
The actor that played Marv, Daniel Petronijevic, was also born in 1981, and

00:39:53.708 --> 00:39:56.082
he doesn't appear to be aged up or aged down in makeup.

00:39:56.146 --> 00:39:58.566
He's just playing his actual 40 year old self.

00:39:58.668 --> 00:40:02.126
Also, Spiral came out in 2021, so it's pretty easy to assume that this is

00:40:02.148 --> 00:40:02.798
when it was set.

00:40:02.884 --> 00:40:05.514
Anyway, Marv is killed in the Subway Trap on July 4th.

00:40:05.562 --> 00:40:08.906
The next day is July 5th, and Zeke is forced to team up with rookie Detective

00:40:08.938 --> 00:40:09.690
William Schenk.

00:40:09.770 --> 00:40:12.846
This is William Emerson, the new Jigsaw, but he changed his name so that

00:40:12.868 --> 00:40:14.010
nobody would make the connection.

00:40:14.090 --> 00:40:17.226
As they delve deeper into the case, they uncover a dark web of corruption

00:40:17.258 --> 00:40:20.206
within the police force, and more and more crooked cops are put into Jigsaw traps.

00:40:20.238 --> 00:40:22.242
Zeke takes the lead on the case.

00:40:22.296 --> 00:40:25.410
They question Bozwick's mourning wife, and during some late night research,

00:40:25.480 --> 00:40:27.902
another cop named Fitch is put into the Finger Trap.

00:40:27.966 --> 00:40:29.422
The next day is July 6th.

00:40:29.486 --> 00:40:32.166
Fitch's fingers are discovered at a freeway underpass, along with a new

00:40:32.188 --> 00:40:35.522
message from the new Jigsaw, and the body is later found at a bread factory.

00:40:35.586 --> 00:40:38.518
Zeke and Schenk investigate a drug dealer who may have ties to the case, and

00:40:38.524 --> 00:40:40.514
they question Zeke's old partner, Dunleavy.

00:40:40.562 --> 00:40:43.542
That night, Zeke's father, a former cop, also goes missing.

00:40:43.606 --> 00:40:46.854
And our last date on the timeline for now is July 7th.

00:40:46.902 --> 00:40:50.042
And I know I've been counting correctly, because we can see the date is 7/7

00:40:50.096 --> 00:40:51.430
on a security camera feed.

00:40:51.510 --> 00:40:54.534
Schenk doesn't show up for work that day, and police receive a new package

00:40:54.582 --> 00:40:56.514
containing skin with Schenk's tattoo.

00:40:56.582 --> 00:40:59.258
A body is discovered at a local butcher shop, and they assume that it's Schenk.

00:40:59.274 --> 00:41:02.206
The police chief is then attacked in the evidence room and put into

00:41:02.228 --> 00:41:03.002
the Wax Trap.

00:41:03.066 --> 00:41:06.426
Zeke continues to search for his dad, but he's kidnapped by someone in a pig mask

00:41:06.458 --> 00:41:09.806
and finds himself in a series of tests in an abandoned soap factory.

00:41:09.918 --> 00:41:13.266
As you can probably guess, I'll refer to this as the Soap Factory Game.

00:41:13.368 --> 00:41:16.834
At the end, he finds Schenk alive, and to his surprise, Schenk wants to team

00:41:16.872 --> 00:41:17.410
up with him.

00:41:17.480 --> 00:41:20.758
His proposal is for Zeke to help him find the dirty cops, and Schenk would

00:41:20.764 --> 00:41:22.578
give them Jigsaw style punishments.

00:41:22.674 --> 00:41:26.146
He brings him to the final test, where Zeke finds his dad in the IV drip trap.

00:41:26.178 --> 00:41:29.602
Zeke must decide between stopping Schenk or freeing his dad.

00:41:29.666 --> 00:41:32.470
In the end, Zeke saves his dad, but Schenk has a backup plan.

00:41:32.540 --> 00:41:35.638
When the SWAT team cuts down the door, it triggers a machine that puppeteers

00:41:35.654 --> 00:41:38.730
Mr. Banks to look like a threat, and they're all forced to shoot him down.

00:41:38.800 --> 00:41:40.906
In all of the commotion, Schenk gets away.

00:41:41.008 --> 00:41:43.822
So there are now at least three Jigsaws running around out there.

00:41:43.876 --> 00:41:48.138
Dr. Gordon, Logan Nelson, and William Emerson, aka William Schenk.

00:41:48.234 --> 00:41:51.806
In the end, there was just one scene that I absolutely couldn't place.

00:41:51.908 --> 00:41:52.670
In Saw 7

00:41:52.740 --> 00:41:56.046
during the survivor support group, we meet a new survivor named Sidney, who

00:41:56.068 --> 00:41:58.282
tells about her experiences in the Lawnmower Trap.

00:41:58.346 --> 00:42:01.298
There's no indication of when this happened, but if I had to put it somewhere,

00:42:01.304 --> 00:42:04.654
I would put it in the first quarter of 2006 before the Classroom Trap

00:42:04.702 --> 00:42:06.030
or the Angel Trap.

00:42:06.110 --> 00:42:09.358
Maybe Amanda put Sidney in the lawnmower trap, and she was frustrated when

00:42:09.384 --> 00:42:12.146
Sidney survived, and that's why she decided to make future traps inescapable. 

00:42:12.178 --> 00:42:15.522
So that's the Saw timeline as it currently stands.

00:42:15.586 --> 00:42:18.422
It's not perfect by any means, but there are really only a few

00:42:18.476 --> 00:42:20.082
major contradictions that can't be explained.

00:42:20.146 --> 00:42:23.018
You could argue that there shouldn't have been HDTVs in some of the

00:42:23.024 --> 00:42:26.634
flashback scenes before HD was popular, but technically it was possible.

00:42:26.752 --> 00:42:29.994
I think after Saw X, there's really no room in the timeline to do anything

00:42:30.032 --> 00:42:30.886
with John Kramer.

00:42:30.918 --> 00:42:33.552
But as Eleanor so eloquently explained,

00:42:33.552 --> 00:42:34.970
-[Eleanor] Jigsaw lives forever.

00:42:34.970 --> 00:42:36.370
-[Eleanor] Through the work of his followers. 

00:42:36.370 --> 00:42:39.258
So it'll be interesting to see what happens with our current surviving Jigsaws 

00:42:39.274 --> 00:42:41.598
and who might take up the mantle next.

00:42:41.684 --> 00:42:45.066
I've got individual analysis episodes on each of John Kramer's devoted followers,

00:42:45.098 --> 00:42:47.162
as well as some other Saw characters.

00:42:47.226 --> 00:42:50.030
You can find them in that playlist on the left for all things Saw

00:42:50.100 --> 00:42:53.230
Make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

00:42:53.300 --> 00:42:55.042
Ring the deathbell for all notifications

00:42:55.066 --> 00:42:57.222
and I'll see you in the next one.

